<title>CHINA: China tobacco industry profits up 16.9 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>China tobacco industry profits up 16.9 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's tobacco industry reported pre-tax profits of 83 billion yuan ($10 billion) in 1996, up 12 billion yuan, or 16.9 percent, from 1995, state media said on Friday.</p>
<p>The area planted under tobacco was expected to remain unchanged at 1.33 million hectares in 1997, state media quoted Ni Yijin, director of the State Tobacco Monopoly Bureau as saying.</p>
<p>Cigarette output in 1997 would remain unchanged from last year, state media said. China produced 34.25 million cartons of cigarettes in 1996, a monopoly official said by telephone.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>--Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
</text>
